(Shafts of morning sunlight cut through colossal carved pillars of Himalayan cedar, sandstone, and molten gold.) Tj
T* (Incense of aged sandalwood and camphor coiled like prayer toward the vaulted ceiling, where constellations of) Tj
T* (the solar dynasty were painted in lapis lazuli. Ayodhya stood unconquered and impregnable, a metropolis where) Tj
T* (poverty was unknown, where every citizen was versed in the Vedas, and where gardens bloomed with perpetual) Tj
T* (spring. The avenues were wide, swept clean with scented water, lined with mansions whose balconies gleamed) Tj
T* (with pearls. Yet in the center of this golden paradise, upon the eight-lion ivory throne, sat King Dasharatha.) Tj
T* (Though his broad shoulders bore the scars of sixty thousand celestial campaigns fought alongside the gods) Tj
T* (against the Asuras, his eyes were sunken hollows of unuttered despair.) Tj
