(King Rama walked the terrace alone in the midnight hour, murmuring to the quiet stars: "The citizens sleep in peace; no thief) Tj
T* (disturbs their rest; no tear falls unavenged. But who can measure the agony of the king’s own heart? The world sees the) Tj
T* (golden crown, the royal umbrella, the fourfold army, and the adoration of millions. They do not see the hollow chest where) Tj
T* (my Sita once rested her head. I banished my life, my soul, my innocence into the wilderness, so that the throne of the) Tj
T* (Ikshvakus might remain beyond reproach. Is this the prize of virtue—to be the loneliest man upon the earth?") Tj
